# MVP Scope

## MVP Goal

The goal of the MVP is to build a working project health dashboard that allows a user to create a software project, track risks and blockers, monitor milestones, and generate a basic weekly status report.

## In Scope

### Project Management

- Create a project
- View all projects
- View project details
- Edit project status
- Assign project health: Green, Yellow, Red

### Risk Management

- Add a risk to a project
- Set risk probability
- Set risk impact
- Calculate risk severity
- Assign a risk owner
- Set mitigation plan
- Update risk status

### Blocker Management

- Add a blocker
- Assign owner
- Set blocker status
- Mark blocker as resolved

### Milestone Tracking

- Add milestones
- Set target dates
- Track completion status

### Status Reporting

- Generate a weekly report based on project data
- Include project health, risks, blockers, milestones, and next steps

## Out of Scope for MVP

- User authentication
- Role-based access control
- Jira integration
- Email notifications
- AI-generated reports
- Advanced analytics
- AWS deployment
- Mobile app
- Multi-tenant workspaces

## Success Criteria

The MVP is successful when a user can:

1. Create a project
2. Add at least one risk
3. Add at least one blocker
4. Add at least one milestone
5. View overall project health
6. Generate a simple weekly status report
